  "slug": "number-coupled-eeef",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published model examine coupling-dependent control of oscillation, synchronisation, and epigenetic state restriction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that feedback and coupling structure, rather than isolated node properties, shape robustness and coherence in regulatory circuits. A published modeling study reports that dynamic condensate assembly enhances the robustness and phase coherence of transcription-translation feedback oscillations. A phase-dependent Kuramoto model, with wavelet feature extraction from Per2::luciferase traces, addresses synchronisation across networks of circadian clocks, a coupling question. A Markov chain model with state-dependent regulatory bias reproduces progressive restriction of epigenetic aging state space in mouse, rat, and bat DNA data, a distinct setting. What is new is explicit convergence on coupling-dependent control across these systems; the items do not establish a single common noise mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-28"
}
